# Scope of the licence, and third-party material

The MIT licence in [LICENSE](LICENSE) covers the analysis code in `scripts/`,
the documentation in `docs/`, and the environment manifests `env.yaml` and
`requirements.txt`.

The following are **not** covered by it.

## Manuscript text and figures

Files under `revision/**/` with the extensions `.tex`, `.md` and
`figures/*.png` are the authors' manuscript material, made available under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0) — the same
licence MDPI applies to the published article.

## MDPI LaTeX template

`revision/*/Definitions/` contains MDPI's own template files (`mdpi.cls`,
`mdpi.bst`, `chicago2.bst`, `journalnames.tex`) together with MDPI, Creative
Commons and ORCID logo artwork. These remain the property of their respective
owners and are included only so that the manuscript can be rebuilt. They are
not licensed for reuse under the terms of this repository.

## Datasets

No dataset is redistributed here. Each corpus must be obtained from its original
source under its own licence — WESAD's EULA prohibits redistribution, and the
Nurse corpus contains participant-level survey rows. See
[data/README.md](data/README.md) for sources, terms and the citation each one
requires.
